## 3. Fixing the Contribution Graph (Missing Greens)

**The Problem:** Your 2025 activity was not showing up on your GitHub profile.
**The Cause:** GitHub only counts contributions if your local email matches your account email AND the work is merged into the **default branch** (which was `master`).

### The Fix

1. **Check Identity:**
```bash
git config user.email

```


2. **Set Identity (if it doesn't match GitHub):**
```bash
git config --global user.email "your-github-email@example.com"

```


3. **Merge the Pull Request:** Click the **"Compare & pull request"** button on GitHub, then click **"Merge pull request"** and **"Confirm merge"**. This moves your work into the default branch, lighting up your green squares.

